            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Sides",
                        "email": "christopher.sides@hpe.com",
                        "username": "csides-hpe"
                    },
                    "message": "This PR resolves an issue with 'TachSensor' sensor records reporting the pwm duty cycle as 'rpm' for fans with no readable tachometer.\n\nAlternatively, instead of reporting a 'calculated RPM' for TachSensors in webui, we can hide TachSensor objects from redfish/webui sensor page by leveraging cooling/cooled_by association handling (PR to do this on the way).\n\nThat method involves connecting fans to the chassis via a cooling/cooled_by relationship called out in an Entity-Manager config, plus adding simple code to TachSensors.cpp to skip adding the 'usual association' records for TachSensor.\n\nFans control still works, but TachSensor objects won't be displayed as chassis sensors in webui."
                }
            ],
