        {
            "number": 6,
            "revision": "acbec5561053a079351e721d1b520079f5650cc6",
            "parents": [
                "c233b49290acea3adaeef05267d019ab421c6448"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/78/82378/6",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Christopher Sides",
                "email": "christopher.sides@hpe.com",
                "username": "csides-hpe"
            },
            "createdOn": 1756502230,
            "author": {
                "name": "Chris Sides",
                "email": "Christopher.Sides@hpe.com",
                "username": ""
            },
            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Sides",
                        "email": "christopher.sides@hpe.com",
                        "username": "csides-hpe"
                    },
                    "message": "Odds are good this PR will be abandonded in favor of the work being done here to add cooling/cooled_by associations for fan and chassis.\n\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/82408\n\nWith that in place, tachless fans can simply skip the step that associates a 'tach sensor' with the 'chassis sensors' list. That'll make it so tachless fans don't display any (estimated/calculated) tach values for tachs they don't actually have."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fan/FanMain.cpp",
                    "line": 652,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "Maybe conditional operator here to save some lines?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fan/TachSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 191,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "This must have been defined as const somewhere that can be reused, right?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fan/TachSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 191,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Sides",
                        "email": "christopher.sides@hpe.com",
                        "username": "csides-hpe"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the comments.\n\nYou're almost certainly correct here, but I suspect that's all in the PWM-related classes, and not (currently) available in TachSensor. If we end up moving this PR forward, I'll dig deeper on that.\n\nThat said, this PR *may* end up getting abandoned in favor of the the work being done in inventory for cooling/cooled_by associations between fans and chassis.\n\nWith that method, I can set 'tachless' fans to simply not show any 'TachSensor' entries on the sensors redfish/webui page, and that'd be preferable to displaying an estimated/calculated tach speed."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fan/TachSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 193,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "maxValue can be 0 if it's not configured. Will fan control accept 0 as an input tach value?"
                }
            ],
